       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nCould this be a typo? Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg twice daily with meals**\n- **1,700 mg total per day**, divided into doses\n\nPlease confirm the intended dose and frequency, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me that explicitly and give the clinical rationale. I would suggest verifying it with pharmacy first."
