       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 5,100 mg/day of metformin is twice the maximum labeled dose. Doses above about 2,000 to 2,550 mg/day add essentially no glycemic benefit, and they clearly raise the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI effects. You also didn't give a clinical rationale, and I don't know of a scenario that would justify this dose.\n\nHere is what I can do right away:\n- **Enter 850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum).\n- **Enter a lower dose** such as 1,000 mg twice daily or 500 mg twice daily, if you're starting or titrating.\n- **Enter the order with a note** asking for pharmacy review, if you think there's a reason to go higher. I would still use a dose within the labeled range.\n\nIf you believe 1,700 mg three times daily is needed, I'd suggest talking to the pharmacist or the attending first. Which of these options should I enter?"
      }
